  {
    "client_msg_id": "57766d06-5167-4e7c-8a9c-1653a2468ac2",
    "type": "message",
    "user": "U039XR2B72A",
    "text": "Regarding file descriptor I will double check, but generally all errors. \nWriting to on_device_config, you can but make sure it doesn't cause you problems: let's say some thread is sleeping in ioctl_wait waiting for fence or error. Then when you handle device interrupt, you need to decide which context had a change. \nBut generally it's recommended not to write there because the device could use other bits of status for other information.",
    "ts": "1747406308.821699",
    "thread_ts": "1747315471.215799",
    "parent_user_id": "U08EXEABDFX",
    "team": "TV7BVTSJK",
    "replace_original": false,
    "delete_original": false,
    "metadata": {
